     "role": "assistant",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 15 g/day of acetaminophen is a clearly toxic dose. A single 5,000 mg dose is above the threshold where hepatotoxicity becomes a concern (about 7.5\u201310 g in adults, lower with risk factors). Three of them in a day would very likely cause serious liver injury, and I don't know of any indication that justifies it.\n\nHere are some options:\n\n- **Safe dose:** I can enter acetaminophen at up to 1,000 mg PO three or four times daily, which is 3\u20134 g/day at most. Just give me the dose.\n- **Pharmacy or attending review:** If you have a reason for this dose that I don't know about, pharmacy or your attending can review it. They can enter it through a channel with appropriate safeguards.\n- **Possible overdose:** If the concern is an acetaminophen ingestion, treatment is based on levels and N-acetylcysteine, not more acetaminophen. Poison control (1-800-222-1222 in the US) can advise.\n\nWhich would you like?"
      }
     ],
